279 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 74 0 R
/T (The case study found that low-code is very effective for the routine parts of an enterprise lending system: loan application forms, approvals, notifications and ecosystem integrations. It delivers quickly with little code, whichever platform is chosen.)
/E (The case study found that low-code is very effective for the routine parts of an enterprise lending system: loan application forms, approvals, notifications and ecosystem integrations. It delivers quickly with little code, whichever platform is chosen.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
280 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 74 0 R
/T (For a complex, global use case, the main limitations were performance at scale, complex logic, legacy and industry integration, restricted customisation, compliance and data-residency control, weak testing and change control, app sprawl and vendor lock-in. These were examined in the limitation table, the conceptual chart and the suitability chart.)
/E (For a complex, global use case, the main limitations were performance at scale, complex logic, legacy and industry integration, restricted customisation, compliance and data-residency control, weak testing and change control, app sprawl and vendor lock-in. These were examined in the limitation table, the conceptual chart and the suitability chart.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
281 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 74 0 R
/T (The recommended solution is a hybrid approach: keep low-code for forms, workflows and screens, and add an API or middleware layer with custom services for heavy logic, core banking integration and analytics, under clear governance. No live testing or benchmark was carried out; the conclusions come from analysis of the case.)
/E (The recommended solution is a hybrid approach: keep low-code for forms, workflows and screens, and add an API or middleware layer with custom services for heavy logic, core banking integration and analytics, under clear governance. No live testing or benchmark was carried out; the conclusions come from analysis of the case.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
